Description: CVE-2026-63383 - evrpc: fix out-of-bounds read in decode_tag_internal
 decode_tag_internal() in event_tagging.c pulls up at most sizeof(number)+1
 bytes from the evbuffer, but then iterated the decoding loop up to the full
 buffer length (`len`) rather than the number of bytes actually made
 contiguous by evbuffer_pullup(). When `len` exceeded sizeof(number)+1 the
 loop advanced the `data` pointer past the pulled-up region, causing an
 out-of-bounds read (CWE-125). This is reachable through the evrpc tag
 decoding path with attacker-controlled input.
 .
 Compute the actual pulled-up length once and bound the decode loop by that
 value so the loop never reads beyond the contiguous region returned by
 evbuffer_pullup().
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/91ed8745eebabdd27592a83d350338a8c4626321
Bug: https://github.com/libevent/libevent/security/advisories/GHSA-fj29-64w6-73h6
Author: libevent maintainers
Last-Update: 2026-08-22
