Description: CVE-2026-63387 - Fix out-of-bounds write in dnsname_to_labels
 An off-by-one error in dnsname_to_labels() in libevent's evdns.c allows a
 one-byte out-of-bounds NUL write past the end of the buffer used by
 evdns_server_request_format_response(). The existing bounds checks used
 strict '>' comparisons, allowing the write offset j to reach buf_len
 exactly, after which the terminating NUL write buf[j++] = 0 lands one byte
 past the end of the buffer. Reachable via the DNS server API by constructing
 a response record whose encoded name reaches offset buf_len-1 before a short
 label is written. This adds an explicit bounds check ((size_t)j >= buf_len)
 before writing the terminating NUL.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/377b9022c3ac61aa4540b5dc4b70c60bf74c663d
Author: Nick Mathewson <nickm@torproject.org>
Last-Update: 2026-08-22
---
--- a/evdns.c
+++ b/evdns.c
@@ -1671,7 +1671,10 @@ dnsname_to_labels(u8 *const buf, size_t buf_len, off_t j,
 	/* the labels must be terminated by a 0. */
 	/* It's possible that the name ended in a . */
 	/* in which case the zero is already there */
-	if (!j || buf[j-1]) buf[j++] = 0;
+	if ((size_t)j >= buf_len)
+		return -2;
+	if (!j || buf[j-1])
+		buf[j++] = 0;
 	return j;
  overflow:
 	return (-2);
Description: CVE-2026-63384 - Fix integer overflow in evtag_unmarshal_header
 On platforms where int is 32 bits, if evtag_unmarshal_header() tried to
 decode a header declaring a payload longer than INT_MAX bytes long, the
 function would return a negative value, which could cause incorrect
 behaviors, incorrect allocations, or denial-of-service (CWE-190).
 This is fixed by rejecting any payload length larger than INT_MAX.
 Fixes GHSA-45c6-qx49-89m8.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/5e3c6ebe342b34c5a9bcf48e9a32ad6708b9c416
Author: Nick Mathewson <nickm@torproject.org>
Last-Update: 2026-08-22
---
--- a/event_tagging.c
+++ b/event_tagging.c
@@ -445,7 +445,7 @@ evtag_unmarshal_header(struct evbuffer *evbuf, ev_uint32_t *ptag)

 	if (decode_tag_internal(ptag, evbuf, 1 /* dodrain */) == -1)
 		return (-1);
-	if (evtag_decode_int(&len, evbuf) == -1)
+	if (evtag_decode_int(&len, evbuf) == -1 || len > INT_MAX)
 		return (-1);

 	if (evbuffer_get_length(evbuf) < len)
--- a/include/event2/tag.h
+++ b/include/event2/tag.h
@@ -64,6 +64,8 @@ void evtag_init(void);
 /**
    Unmarshals the header and returns the length of the payload

+   Returns an error if the payload length is above INT_MAX.
+
    @param evbuf the buffer from which to unmarshal data
    @param ptag a pointer in which the tag id is being stored
    @returns -1 on failure or the number of bytes in the remaining payload.
Description: CVE-2026-63382 - fix HTTP request smuggling in evhttp
 Restrict the acceptable combinations of Content-Length and Transfer-Encoding
 headers and parse Transfer-Encoding per RFC to prevent HTTP request smuggling
 (GHSA-q39v-w2g7-gr8j). This rejects requests that supply both Content-Length
 and Transfer-Encoding, a duplicated Content-Length, a duplicated
 Transfer-Encoding, a multi-valued Transfer-Encoding where "chunked" is not the
 final coding, and any "chunked" coding that is not the last transfer-coding.
 New helpers evhttp_find_unique_header(), evhttp_str_is_chunked_(),
 evhttp_check_transfer_encoding_() and evhttp_validate_len_and_encoding_() are
 added, and the chunked-body flag is now derived from the validated headers.
 .
 Additionally, HTTP chunk framing is parsed with EVBUFFER_EOL_CRLF_STRICT
 instead of EVBUFFER_EOL_CRLF so that a bare LF is no longer accepted as a
 chunk-size line terminator (RFC 9112).
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/ac38703b2d312200c4f967f02936af0118d384a0
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/10abb34b8dc3e1184de315dd261ce4b77563cda6
